{"id": "EUVD-2026-104301", "enisaUuid": "3496d48b-90c4-3293-801b-7edeca5afb84", "description": "Libdisplay-info 0.4.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the DisplayID v2 section parser in displayid2.c that allows attackers to read past the EDID buffer via oversized data block lengths. Attackers can supply a crafted EDID from a malicious monitor, KVM, capture device, or file to over-advance the parse cursor and crash applications.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:34:25", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libdisplay-info-displayid-datablock-overrun-oob-read", "https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/emersion/libdisplay-info/-/blob/0.4.0/displayid2.c#L84-L143", "https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/emersion/libdisplay-info", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libdisplay-info-0.4.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-displayid-v2-parser"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qvww-h55c-pg37", "CVE-2026-112272"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ed346a26-df56-370e-ac5a-dce7a322d581", "product": {"name": "libdisplay-info", "vendor": {"name": "emersion"}}, "product_version": "0.4.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1ade886f-6dc1-30a2-8ecf-a505500807e9", "vendor": {"name": "emersion"}}], "isExploited": false}